# rules: swift-insecure-random-for-secret
# languages: swift
# fixture: swift/CWE-338.swift
# from: CWE-338 (Weak PRNG), CWE-330, swift/lang/crypto/insecure-random.yaml,
#       MASVS-CRYPTO-3
#
# `Int.random(in:)`, `arc4random_uniform` and the rest draw from
# `SystemRandomNumberGenerator`, which Apple documents as suitable for general
# use and explicitly does *not* guarantee to be cryptographically secure. For a
# shuffle, a retry jitter or a random colour that is exactly the right tool.
# For anything an attacker would like to guess it is the whole of the
# vulnerability, and `SecRandomCopyBytes` is the same amount of code.
#
# The rule this replaces reported every draw in the program. That is the
# failure mode this corpus is most careful about: a rule that fires on a card
# shuffle teaches people to switch the rule off, and then it is worse than not
# having been written. Over any real app the old rule's output is almost
# entirely animation timings and test data.
#
# What makes the difference is the *name the result is given*. A programmer who
# calls it `sessionToken`, `nonce` or `otpSecret` has said what it is for, and
# that is the one piece of evidence in the syntax about which kind of draw this
# is. It is the same reading that makes the credential rules work, used the
# other way round: there the name makes the rule look and the value makes it
# report, and here there is no value to read, so the name decides.
#
# A draw that is passed straight to something rather than bound to a name is
# not reported. That is a real gap and it is the quiet direction.

[ "let $N = $R", "let $N: $T = $R", "var $N = $R", "var $N: $T = $R" ] as $binds
| "(?i)token|nonce|salt|^iv$|secret|key$|passw|otp|challenge|session"
  + "|verifier|csrf|state$|seed" as $namesASecret
| "\\b(?:Int|UInt|UInt32|UInt64|Double|Float|Bool)\\.random\\s*\\("
  + "|\\barc4random\\b|\\barc4random_uniform\\s*\\(|\\brandom\\s*\\(\\s*\\)"
  + "|\\bdrand48\\s*\\(|\\brandomElement\\s*\\(|SystemRandomNumberGenerator"
  as $guessableDraw
| scan_ast("*.swift"; $binds) as $all
| ( $all | of($binds)
    | where_capture("N"; $namesASecret)
    | where_capture("R"; $guessableDraw)
    | focus("R") )
| finding("swift-insecure-random-for-secret";
    "$N is drawn from a generator that is not promised to be unpredictable; "
    + "SecRandomCopyBytes is the same amount of code")
| report
